  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/bc6b71d1fe69abd34dbd939dc62ede5201b75713e25456cf084e889bc44f449e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.4$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/4a1fd7069abaa3b3fa4d9c286773d226798bf3ad565e85663cab44557fd635c1.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/260e8e959ca95a029a98bd4102106a66df418ea73c0640398c8fdebfdbf812f6.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true.",
